hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1594","I am Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala. Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed and Muhammad bin Ajlan. H Saeed bin Abdul Rahman, narrated to us by Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan. It was also narrated by Sa’id, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id. H Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us. Yahya bin Hakim told us, Hammad bin Masada told us, they said: Ibn Ajlan told us, this is the hadith of Abdul Jabbar, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Yahya Ibn Hibban, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, on the authority of Muawiyah, said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “I have appeared, so do not You hasten with me to bow and prostrate, for whatever I precede you with when I kneel, you will overtake me with it when I rise, and whatever I precede you with when I kneel, you will overtake me with it when I rise. I prostrated, and you will overtake me with it when I rise.” Abu Bakr said: Al-Makhzoumi did not mention in the hadith of Yahya: “And whatever I will precede you with when I prostrate,” etc. Yahya bin Hakim said: “Indeed, I have acted or acted as a sinner.”"
